Fillets: a chain rounded past a wall's convex corner that is rounded with
less than the radius (mitcad#343).

The case: a part's underside outline (a plane U) rounded with 0.5, its
side walls square to U, its front wall leaning 15 degrees over U (the
edge with U acute), the vertical corners between them rounded with 0.3.
The chain runs line, corner arc (U with the corner's cylinder K), line.
No ball of the radius rolls round K: its centre would have to turn back
about K's axis. OCCT walked the chain over the arc anyway, and the
approximation of the walk, which runs backwards there, threw while it
was stored (StoreData). The bodies stored in the files stop both lines'
roundings where their axes cross, at the ball C that touches U and both
walls, and close the corner with a vertex blend and a torus.

- ChFi3d_Builder::SplitAtTightCorners (new, at the start of Compute): a
  contour of constant radius R on convex edges whose chain has an arc
  between a plane U and a cylinder K of radius below R, between two lines
  whose other faces are planes tangent to K (K's axis inside both), one
  of them (Wp) square to the other line, the other (Wo) square to U or
  leaning over it, is split there: the runs of edges between such arcs
  become contours of their own, their ends at the arcs of status
  ChFiDS_Tangent, the arcs left out.
- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformTightCorners (new, before the corners at
  vertices): for each such arc, C is R inside U, Wp and Wo (where the
  rounding axes Lp along Wp and Lo along Wo cross) and D its contact on
  U. With rho = R - rk (rk K's radius), np Wp's outward normal, ep the
  direction along Lp towards the corner and e0 Wo's outward normal: the
  vertex blend V is C + sin t A(u) + cos t R n (n U's outward normal),
  A(u) the arc of radius rk about O = C + rho np + rho ep in the plane of
  C parallel to U, from Q (towards np) to M (towards ep): a rational
  biquadratic patch, tangent to both roundings along its ellipses D-Q and
  D-M, the point D its degenerated edge. Where Wo leans over U, K turns
  about Lo from e0 to ep (the torus T about Lo, its tube K's radius about
  the circle of radius rho in the plane square to Lo through Wo's edge
  with K): T meets V along its last meridian Q-M, Lo's rounding along an
  arc of radius R, Wp along an arc of radius rho, and cuts K along K's
  section through Wo's contact. The roundings end at D and Q (Lp's), D
  and Wo's contact on its edge with K (Lo's); V and T are corner stripes
  on the roundings' surfaces (and Wp), as the three-edge corner's patch.
  The transitions follow from the side each face keeps, seen along the
  normal of its surface. Where Wo is square to U there is no torus: V's
  arc is K's section, which cuts K.
- ChFi3d_Builder::SplitKPart: at the last end of such a contour no
  piece's contact runs into a face at the end; all pieces are kept, as at
  the first end (before, all were dropped and the analytic rounding was
  walked).

On the design's body before the item (the outline's five edges): valid,
197 faces as the file's, every face on the stored body's within 0.002 mm
both ways, the change of volume -1.5382 against the file's -1.5432 mm3;
before, the fillet failed. Synthetic: a block's bottom outline rounded with
0.5 past front corners rounded with 0.3, the front wall square to the
bottom and leaning 15 degrees over it, and the whole outline with all
four corners rounded: valid, the vertex blends exact, the torus where the
wall leans, the material taken within 1e-6 mm3 of the integral where the
walls are square.

Upstream: new.
